{"id":"cmn-t1-0001","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.eight","domain":2,"text_native":"八","text_romanized":"bā","text_english":"Eight.","source_caption":"8","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0002","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.five","domain":2,"text_native":"五","text_romanized":"wǔ","text_english":"Five.","source_caption":"5","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Five is where most of these languages change to a different counting pattern, and knowing that in advance is the point of learning them in order.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0003","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.four","domain":2,"text_native":"四","text_romanized":"sì","text_english":"Four.","source_caption":"4","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0004","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.nine","domain":2,"text_native":"九","text_romanized":"jiǔ","text_english":"Nine.","source_caption":"9","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0005","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.one","domain":2,"text_native":"一","text_romanized":"yī","text_english":"One.","source_caption":"1","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Counting from one upward in order, because a traveller counts by reciting rather than by arithmetic.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0006","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.seven","domain":2,"text_native":"七","text_romanized":"qī","text_english":"Seven.","source_caption":"7","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0007","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.six","domain":2,"text_native":"六","text_romanized":"liù","text_english":"Six.","source_caption":"6","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0008","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.ten","domain":2,"text_native":"十","text_romanized":"shí","text_english":"Ten.","source_caption":"10","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The first number past the counting pattern in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0009","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.three","domain":2,"text_native":"三","text_romanized":"sān","text_english":"Three.","source_caption":"3","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0010","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.two","domain":2,"text_native":"二 (二) (两 (兩) liǎng is used when specifying quantities)","text_romanized":"èr","text_english":"Two.","source_caption":"2","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0011","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"〇 (〇) / 零 (零)","text_romanized":"líng","text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0012","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"买单","text_romanized":"mǎidān","text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0013","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"信用卡","text_romanized":"xìn yòng kǎ","text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"credit card","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0014","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"这个多少钱？","text_romanized":"zhège duōshǎo qián?","text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0015","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.pay-cash","domain":3,"text_native":"现金","text_romanized":"xiàn jīn","text_english":"Cash, please.","source_caption":"cash","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Worth having even where cards are universal, because it changes what you are offered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0016","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"便宜","text_romanized":"piányi","text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0017","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"太贵了。","text_romanized":"tài guì le","text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"That's too expensive.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0018","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"money.exchange-rate","domain":3,"text_native":"汇率","text_romanized":"huìlǜ","text_english":"What is the exchange rate?","source_caption":"exchange rate","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Often answered by pointing at a board rather than spoken.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0019","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"厕所在哪里？","text_romanized":"Cèsuǒ zài nǎlǐ?","text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Where is the toilet?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0020","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"水","text_romanized":"shuĭ","text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0021","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"直走","text_romanized":"zhízŏu","text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"Go straight","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0022","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"左转","text_romanized":"zuǒ zhuǎn","text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0023","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"右转","text_romanized":"yòu zhuǎn","text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0024","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"我想退房。","text_romanized":"Wǒ xiǎng tuìfáng","text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0025","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"我需要医生。","text_romanized":"wǒ xūyào yīshēng","text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0026","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"我受伤了。","text_romanized":"wǒ shòushāng le","text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0027","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"不要碰我！","text_romanized":"búyào pèng wǒ","text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0028","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"这是紧急情况。","text_romanized":"zhèshì jǐnjí qíngkuàng","text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0029","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"不要打扰我。","text_romanized":"búyào dǎrǎo wǒ","text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0030","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"我迷路了。","text_romanized":"wǒ mílù le","text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0031","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"我可以打个电话吗？","text_romanized":"wǒ kěyǐ dǎ ge diànhuà ma?","text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0032","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"我要叫警察了。","text_romanized":"wǒ yào jiào jǐngchá le","text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"cmn-t1-0033","lang":"cmn","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"住手！小偷！","text_romanized":"zhùshǒu! xiǎotōu","text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Chinese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chinese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
